 "procurementBestPractice": {
  "Need & Planning": "Check the shared contract database and market before launching a new procedure. Use long-term planning to reduce repeated procurement effort.",
  "Thresholds & Procedure": "If the estimate is close to €184,000, use the international route rather than risk exceeding the threshold later.",
  "Tender Design": "Download a fresh template at the start of each procurement process because templates are updated over time.",
  "Launch & Publication": "Publish at a sensible time and give suppliers a deadline proportionate to the complexity of the tender.",
  "Evaluation": "Write clear, exhaustive reasons for technical/quality scores; strong documentation makes later enquiries and audits easier.",
  "Contract Management": "Use reminders and proactive supplier communication before deadlines rather than reacting after a missed delivery date.",
  "Filing & Audit Trail": "Archive as the process runs, not at the end. This preserves a cleaner and more reliable audit trail."
 },
